Wands of death will not kill demons -- they aren't alive in the first
place! 

My favourite way of getting rid of Demogorgon in Slash'Em is to burn
Elbereth on the upstairs and then wake him up from distance.  My
favourite method of waking him up is to use a tame (or peaceful)
(master) mind flyer.  Just wait, and Demo will teleport next to you.  It
may take a while, though.

Ways you can make yourself feel more secure: Use =oLevitation on the
Elbereth (although burned texts haven't become wiped off in [S] for me).
Hit Demo with a potion of paralysis, *if* you have free action.  Use
cockatrice corpse, with the usual precautions.  Know "cure sickness"
with 0% fail rate.  Have !oFHs ready.

If you haven't got a (m)mf pet, you could creep closer to Demogorgon,
burn Elbereth, wake him up (tin whistles, exploding yellow lights?, zap
a /oDigging through the last wall), then level-teleport to the upper
level (you've got teleport control) and come again downstairs (where
you've burned Elbereth already).  Then you can proceed as above. :>

Oh, and, I would advise against (m)mf pets on the Wizard's tower top
level...  You don't want to wake Rodney up before you're on the level
yourself.  (If (m)mfs can't wake Rodney up, please correct me.)

